      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 2.79,
          "en": "So now that we revisited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.79,
          "end": 7.53,
          "en": "this important concept of Server and Client Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.53,
          "end": 9.39,
          "en": "which is really important to understand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.39,
          "end": 13.05,
          "en": "it's not too tricky to use, actually, as you saw,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.05,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "but it's important to be aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 18.84,
          "en": "of these two different kinds of components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.84,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "Now that we did that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 24.45,
          "en": "we can dive back into routing-related features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.45,
          "end": 28.65,
          "en": "and explore another special kind of route you can set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.65,
          "end": 31.65,
          "en": "when working with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 34.32,
          "en": "And the kind of route I wanna explore next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.32,
          "end": 37.443,
          "en": "is a so-called interceptor route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 40.38,
          "en": "Now, how does that work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.38,
          "end": 44.13,
          "en": "Well, let's say here in our news slug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.13,
          "end": 47.04,
          "en": "we actually wanna make that image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.04,
          "end": 49.71,
          "en": "that belongs to a news item clickable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.71,
          "end": 54.15,
          "en": "So that we show it on a separate screen, a separate page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 58.383,
          "en": "that shows us that image as a full-screen image, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.49,
          "end": 61.17,
          "en": "To achieve this, we can, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 63.6,
          "en": "add a new nested path here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.6,
          "end": 66.15,
          "en": "inside of that dynamic slug folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.15,
          "end": 67.65,
          "en": "And we could name it image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.65,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "Obviously, the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "And in there we can add a page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 76.08,
          "en": "and then export our component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.08,
          "end": 77.907,
          "en": "which I'll name ImagePage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 82.953,
          "en": "Now in there, I then wanna output that image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 88.02,
          "en": "And to do that, I'll add a div with a className",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.02,
          "end": 90.753,
          "en": "of fullscreen-image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.68,
          "end": 94.713,
          "en": "And then in that div, I wanna output the image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.61,
          "end": 98.58,
          "en": "And of course, now we need to find out which image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 100.65,
          "en": "for which article should be shown here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.65,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "and therefore, I'll actually accept this params property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 107.64,
          "en": "or I'll extract that params property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.64,
          "end": 109.143,
          "en": "from the incoming props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.16,
          "end": 112.62,
          "en": "which will give me access to that select,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.62,
          "end": 116.94,
          "en": "because nested routes inside of some dynamic route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.94,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "also will have access to that dynamic route parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 124.41,
          "en": "so to this slug parameter, in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.41,
          "end": 129.18,
          "en": "So this nested image page can extract this news item slug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 133.29,
          "en": "by simply accessing params.slug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 137.883,
          "en": "just as we did it directly on the dynamic route page itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.17000000000002,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "Therefore, of course, we can also copy the logic from there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 148.52,
          "en": "including this not found check to get a specific news item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.59,
          "end": 152.1,
          "en": "like this, and not found must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 155.043,
          "en": "from next/navigation in order to be available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.45,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "And we can then use the news item to output the actual image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 165.32999999999998,
          "en": "so we can construct the source of the image dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.32999999999998,
          "end": 170.07,
          "en": "It's stored in the images/news folder in the public folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 170.07,
          "end": 175.07,
          "en": "and then the image name is stored in that news item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 178.05,
          "en": "There we'll have a image property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.05,
          "end": 180.99,
          "en": "And of course, DUMMY_NEWS also must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.99,
          "end": 184.11,
          "en": "in order to be available in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.11,
          "end": 186.063,
          "en": "So these imports must be added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 187.71,
          "end": 190.44,
          "en": "With that, we have this image path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 190.44,
          "end": 193.92,
          "en": "and the alt text can, again, be newsItem.title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 193.92,
          "end": 196.023,
          "en": "for example, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 197.46,
          "end": 198.84,
          "en": "And of course, newsItem slug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.84,
          "end": 202.44,
          "en": "is what I should use here in this check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.44,
          "end": 205.89,
          "en": "Okay, so with that, we're then outputting that image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.89,
          "end": 208.44,
          "en": "Now in order to get to this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 208.44,
          "end": 212.31,
          "en": "we can go to the dynamic news detail page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 212.31,
          "end": 216.27,
          "en": "so the page.js filed directly in the slug folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.27,
          "end": 221.27,
          "en": "and then wrap this image here with a link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.37,
          "end": 223.62,
          "en": "So we can use the link component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 223.62,
          "end": 226.8,
          "en": "which is imported from next/link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 226.8,
          "end": 231.32999999999998,
          "en": "and wrap that around the image like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.32999999999998,
          "end": 234.21,
          "en": "and set the path of that link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 234.21,
          "end": 239.14,
          "en": "equal to /news/newsItem.slug/image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 243.81,
          "end": 248.81,
          "en": "That's the path that will get us to this page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 249,
          "end": 251.28,
          "en": "Because that's inside of the news folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 251.28,
          "end": 254.16,
          "en": "then this dynamic slug folder and then the image folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 254.16,
          "end": 259.16,
          "en": "So the path is slash, news, slash, the slug, slash, image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 261.3,
          "end": 265.08,
          "en": "If we save that and we are on a news item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 265.08,
          "end": 267.69,
          "en": "we should therefore be able to click that image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 267.69,
          "end": 270.18,
          "en": "and we should see it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 270.18,
          "end": 272.79,
          "en": "So that seems to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 272.79,
          "end": 276.27,
          "en": "but of course, this is now nothing new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 276.27,
          "end": 278.58,
          "en": "I mean, the only new thing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 278.58,
          "end": 282.33,
          "en": "is that we have a nested path inside of a dynamic path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 282.33,
          "end": 284.25,
          "en": "and yeah, that is nice to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 284.25,
          "end": 287.43,
          "en": "and something you will definitely need from time to time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 287.43,
          "end": 290.73,
          "en": "But that's not this intercepting route feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 290.73,
          "end": 291.65999999999997,
          "en": "I mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 291.65999999999997,
          "end": 294.483,
          "en": "Instead, that's what we'll explore next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
